    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92586" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥοδίζω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥόδον</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be like the rose</i>,
				<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				15.677e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῇ ὀσμῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dsc.
					1.13
				</span></i>
			; in colour, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Gp.</u>
				14.16.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> trans.,
				<i>scent with roses</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς συνθέσεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thphr.
					<u>Od.</u>
					47
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δέρμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.Aphr.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					1.12
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>deck</i> a person's grave <i>with roses</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>BCH</u>
				24.415
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Bithynia</span>):—
				Pass.
			, <i>to have one's grave decked with roses</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CIG</u>
				3754
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Nicaea</span>).</div>
